; Gunslinger trash objects -- the wrapper / bottle / blister the use animation throws away.
; Values are GS's, verbatim from its per-item base.ltx files. GS keeps each one next to its item;
; ours live together because our item folders only hold overrides, not full item definitions.
;
; throw_dir       left | right | forward | back, taken from the CAMERA at the moment of the throw
; throw_offset_*  spawn point relative to the camera: x along cam_dir, y along cam_top, z along cam_right
; throw_impulse_z strength of the push; throw_impulse_y the vertical component of its direction
; Defaults when a key is absent (gwr_eatable.script): offsets -0.1 / 0.2 / 0, impulse 50, impulse_y 0.05.

[medkit_trash]:gwr_base_trash
visual              = gwr\equipment\medkit\medkit_trash.ogf
throw_dir           = right
throw_offset_y      = -0.6
throw_offset_x      = -0.2
throw_offset_z      = 0.6
throw_impulse_y     = -90
throw_impulse_z     = 180

[medkit_army_trash]:medkit_trash

[medkit_scientic_trash]:medkit_trash

